WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.287
The term self-attention tells us where the information comes from.

00:00:04.287 --> 00:00:11.012
In self-attention, Q, K, and V are all derived from the same input sequence.

00:00:11.012 --> 00:00:15.132
That is why the PyTorch call can pass x three times:

00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:16.997
attention of x to x using information from x.

00:00:16.997 --> 00:00:23.202
The layer then applies different learned projections internally.

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:26.062
Cross-attention changes the source.

00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:32.527
In an encoder-decoder model, for example, the decoder may create Queries from its current hidden states while

00:00:32.527 --> 00:00:36.007
the Keys and Values come from the encoder output.

00:00:36.007 --> 00:00:44.077
That lets the decoder ask, in effect, “Which parts of the encoded input are useful for generating the

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:49.812
next output token?” Keep the distinction simple: self-attention mixes information within one sequence;

00:00:49.812 --> 00:00:54.697
cross-attention lets one representation attend to another source.

00:00:54.697 --> 00:00:59.967
This difference becomes important when we compare encoder-only, decoder-only,

00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:02.080
and encoder-decoder architectures.
